Since we're only dealing with directories (mkdir), X always equals x. So X → x.

And permission-copy (u, g, o as permissions):
"Permission copying copies the source class's ordinary read/write/search bits to the selected classes."

So `u+r` means "add to the selected who the read bits that u currently has". Since we're working with directories, this is just the r bit of the u class.

